            "source_snippet": "import sys\nimport math\n\ndef find_min_i(n, k, A0):\n    # Calculate the prefix sum of A0\n    prefix_sum = [0] * (n + 1)\n    for i in range(n):\n        prefix_sum[i + 1] = prefix_sum[i] + A0[i]\n    \n    # If any element in A0 is already >= k, return 0\n    if max(A0) >= k:\n        return 0\n    \n    # If the sum of all elements in A0 is < k, we need at least one more iteration\n    if prefix_sum[-1] < k:\n        return 1\n    \n    # Binary search to find the minimum i\n    low, high = 1, n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        # Calculate A^mid\n        A_mid = [prefix_sum[i] - prefix_sum[i - 1] for i in range(1, n + 1)]\n        for _ in range(mid - 1):\n            A_mid = [sum(A_mid[:i]) for i in range(1, n + 1)]\n        \n        if max(A_mid) >= k:\n            high = mid\n        else:\n            low = mid + 1\n    \n    return low\n\n# Read input\ninput = sys.stdin.read\ndata = input().split()\nn = int(data[0])\nk = int(data[1])\nA0 = list(map(int, data[2:]))\n\n# Find and print the result\nresult = find_min_i(n, k, A0)\nprint(result)",
